concept raw_heredocs {
  name     = "Raw Heredocs"
  summary  = "Single-quoted opening tag takes the body verbatim — no escapes, no interpolation."
  related  = [strings, string_literals, string_escapes, heredocs, string_interpolation, expressions]
  audience = :both
  body {
    h2 "Raw heredocs"
    p <<PROSE
A **raw heredoc** uses a single-quoted opening tag and takes the body verbatim —
no escapes, no interpolation, just literal bytes. Ideal for LaTeX, regexes, code
samples with backslashes, or anything where you do not want WCL touching the
contents. Common leading whitespace is still stripped.
PROSE
    code "wcl" { source = <<'SRC'
regex = <<'RAW'
\d{3}-\d{4}
RAW

latex = <<'TEX'
\frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}
TEX
SRC
    }
  }
}
